            <ArticleTitle>Tardive dyskinesia and chronic pain.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>167-70</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Psychotropic drugs are frequently used to treat chronic pain. Tardive dyskinesia is a serious complication of such therapy, but is not mentioned in the pain literature. Two cases are reported and the implications discussed.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
